# Parking workflow — agent reference

Canonical spec for the **parking broadcast-and-claim lifecycle**. Parking keeps its own status
machine and its own edge functions — it is **never** routed through the property
`workflowOrchestrator.ts` / `statusMachine.ts` (see `[[booking-workflow]]`). Design history and
locked decisions: `docs/workflow/done/parking-e2e-phase1-overview.md` and its companion
docs in `docs/workflow/done/` (status-workflow, host-broadcast-notifications, guest-request-realtime-status,
bookings-page-updates, phase0-registration-dimensions). Later phases: `docs/workflow/planned/parking-e2e-later-phases.md`.

## Status graph

```
PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE → PENDING_PAYMENT | NO_HOST_AVAILABLE | CANCELLED
PENDING_PAYMENT         → PENDING_REVIEW | PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE | CANCELLED
PENDING_REVIEW          → READY_FOR_CHECKIN | CANCELLED
READY_FOR_CHECKIN       → COMPLETED | CANCELLED
NO_HOST_AVAILABLE       → (terminal)
CANCELLED               → (terminal)
COMPLETED               → (terminal)
```

`parkingStatusMachine.ts` is the source of truth (`canTransition` / `availableTransitions`),
mirrored client-side in `ui/src/features/dashboard/parking/lib/parkingWorkflow.ts` (keep both in
sync manually — no shared import between server/client bundles).
`transition-parking-booking/index.ts` explicitly **rejects** any transition where `fromStatus`
is `PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE` or `PENDING_PAYMENT` — both only resolve via their own dedicated
functions below, never the generic transition endpoint.

**`PENDING_PAYMENT` (Phase 3) sits between claim and confirmation** — Accept no longer means
confirmed. A host's Accept sets `PENDING_PAYMENT` (not `PENDING_REVIEW`); the guest must pay
before the booking is truly confirmed. `PENDING_REVIEW` still means "paid & confirmed," its
meaning from Phase 1/2 is unchanged — only what precedes it changed. See "Payment (Phase 3)"
below.

## The broadcast round (PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE)

1. **Submit** (`submit-parking-booking-request`, **guest-authenticated since Phase 3** —
   `serveAuthenticated`, was `servePublic`; the client-side Reserve/form flows already required
   guest sign-in before this endpoint was ever called, this just verifies it server-side too):
   stamps `guest_auth_user_id` on the row from the caller's JWT (ownership check for
   pay-now/cancel, and the anti-spam identity for a future fast-follow). **No hard check that
   `guestEmail` matches the caller's own email** — the admin dashboard's "New booking" modal
   legitimately reuses this same endpoint to submit on a guest's behalf (host authenticated,
   guest's email in the body); `guest_auth_user_id` is the real ownership binding, not
   `guestEmail`. **Known gap**: an admin-submitted booking's `guest_auth_user_id` is the host's
   own id, so the actual guest can't self-serve pay/cancel it later unless signed in as that
   same host account — not solved in Phase 3, see the org bookings route guide. Resolves the
   first ranked batch
   (`parkingBroadcast.ts#resolveNextParkingBatch` → `findParkingBroadcastCandidates` — same
   `organization_id`, `status = 'ACTIVE'`, `accepted_vehicle_types @> [...]`, no
   date-overlapping/turnover-buffer-violating booking — then `parkingBroadcastRanking.ts#
rankAndDedupeParkingCandidates` and a `PARKING_BATCH_SIZE` slice; see "Ranked batched dispatch"
   below). Zero candidates after ranking/cap/dedupe → **422 `no_parking_available`, no row
   inserted**. Otherwise inserts a `guest_submissions` row at `PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE` with
   `parking_id = null`, `parking_broadcast_batch_number = 1`, and `parking_pinned_id` set only
   if the guest requested one specific listing directly (not an org-wide search — see below),
   and fans out (`fanOutParkingBroadcast`): one `parking_booking_broadcasts` row per candidate
   (stamped `batch_number` + `host_gross_at_broadcast`) + Telegram + per-recipient email (never
   BCC). **If the fan-out insert itself throws**, the booking row is rolled back (deleted) and
   the guest gets a 500 to retry cleanly — never leave an orphaned `PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE` row
   with zero broadcast rows.
2. **TTL**: 15 min if check-in is today (Asia/Manila), else 1 hr (`parkingBroadcastTtlMs`) —
   **per batch**, not per whole search. Re-applied fresh on every batch advance.
3. **Claim** (`claim-parking-booking`, host, `verifyParkingTeamAccess(..., 'bookings:edit')`
   scoped to the specific `parkingId`): first-Accept-wins is enforced by a single guarded
   `UPDATE guest_submissions ... WHERE id = $bookingId AND status = 'PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE'`.
   **This status-guarded UPDATE on the booking row is the actual source of truth for the
   win condition** — the broadcast-row pre-check (`response = 'pending'`) is a fast-fail UX
   optimization only, not a second authority; a concurrent claim/decline/expire always loses
   the race at the `guest_submissions.status` guard, so it can never double-win even if the
   broadcast-row pre-check briefly disagrees. A losing claim gets `409 already_claimed`.
   Optional endorsement note (host-authored, shown to guest after Accept; ≤500 chars in the
   UI, ≤2000 server-side). **Sets `PENDING_PAYMENT`** (not `PENDING_REVIEW`) with a fresh
   `parking_payment_expires_at` (same TTL asymmetry via `parkingBroadcastTtlMs`), and emails the
   guest `sendParkingAwaitingPaymentEmail` (not the confirmation email — that now fires on
   payment success, see below).
4. **Decline** (`decline-parking-booking`, host, same access check): marks the caller's
   broadcast row `declined`. If it was the **last `pending` row in the current batch**, calls
   `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch` (see below) — never terminates directly.
5. **Expire** (`expire-parking-broadcasts`, cron): sweeps bookings past
   `parking_broadcast_expires_at`, marks that batch's still-`pending` rows `expired`, then also
   calls `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`. **Scheduling**:
   `public.sync_parking_broadcast_expire_cron_job()`
   (migration `20261018120000_parking_broadcast_expire_cron.sql`) — see
   `docs/archive/operations/scheduled-jobs-and-testing.md` for activation.

All terminal-or-advancing transitions funnel through the same guarded-UPDATE idempotency
pattern (claim / decline-all-in-batch / expire), which is also what makes the guest's final
"no host available" email exactly-once — never add a second write path to
`guest_submissions.status` or `parking_broadcast_batch_number` for this state.

## Ranked batched dispatch (Phase 2)

Replaces the old "notify every eligible candidate at once" with a Grab-style ranked, batched
offer. Locked constants (not admin-configurable in v1): `PARKING_BATCH_SIZE = 3`,
`PARKING_TURNOVER_BUFFER_MINUTES = 30` (both in `parkingBroadcastRanking.ts`).

- **Turnover buffer**: a same-day back-to-back (new check-in date == an existing booking's
  checkout date on the same slot, or vice versa) is not a date-range overlap but still needs
  ≥30 min between the two bookings. Sourced from the **listing's own standard check-in/
  check-out time** — `parkings.settings.checkInTime`/`checkOutTime` (already stored, already
  editable in `ParkingDetailsSection.tsx`, defaults `14:00`/`12:00`) — via
  `minutesBetweenTimes()` (`cleaningBuffer.ts`, the same helper the property vertical's
  same-day cleaning buffer uses). **Not** guest-selected times — the guest form only collects
  dates, never per-booking times.
- **Price ranking**: `computeParkingHostGross` averages nightly `host_gross` across the stay
  (weekday/weekend mix + `parking_pricing_date_overrides`, via `loadParkingPricing`). Ascending
  sort; **tie-break is `parkings.created_at` ascending** (earliest-listed spot wins) — a
  deliberate choice, not insertion order.
- **Guest rate cap (D5, live config since Phase 4)**: `resolveParkingPlatformSettings()`
  (`parkingPlatformSettings.ts`) resolves `guestRateWeekday`/`guestRateWeekend` from the
  super-admin-configurable `platform_parking_settings` singleton — a candidate priced above the
  cap for any night in the stay is **excluded from the pool entirely**, not ranked last. Falls
  back to a flat ₱400 stub only if that row is somehow missing (shouldn't happen — the
  migration seeds it).
- **Multi-spot host dedupe**: `resolvePrimaryHostKey` — earliest active `parking_members` row
  with edit access (same predicate `resolveParkingHostRecipients` uses), else the org owner.
  Two candidates sharing a key collapse to the cheaper one.
- **Pinned requests stay single-round**: when the guest requests one specific listing directly
  (`parkingId` in the submit payload → `parking_pinned_id` set), `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`
  never expands the search to other org parkings once that one candidate's batch is exhausted —
  it terminates, matching pre-batching Phase 1 behavior. Only org-wide searches
  (`parking_pinned_id` null) advance through multiple batches.
- **`advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`** (`parkingBroadcastExpireCron.ts`) is the single shared
  brain for "this batch is fully resolved, what now" — called from both decline-all-in-batch and
  TTL expiry. Race-safe via a guarded UPDATE on
  `status = 'PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE' AND parking_broadcast_batch_number = fromBatchNumber`: only
  the first caller to resolve a given batch applies (advance to `fromBatchNumber + 1` with a
  fresh TTL, or terminate to `NO_HOST_AVAILABLE`); a losing concurrent call just no-ops. **Never
  reimplement this guard per-caller.**

## Payment (Phase 3/4)

`PENDING_PAYMENT` resolves exactly three ways, all funneled through
`parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts`:

- **Guest pays**: `create-parking-payment-checkout` (guest-authenticated) lazily creates a
  PayMongo Payment Link on "Pay now" click — reuses an existing `pending`
  `parking_payment_transactions` row if one exists (idempotent across repeated clicks), else
  computes amounts via `computeParkingPaymentAmounts`, which (Phase 4) walks each occupied
  night individually and sums the guest rate and host rate per night by weekday/weekend
  classification (guest side from `resolveParkingPlatformSettings()`, host side from
  `loadParkingPricing()` including date overrides) — **per-night-prorated, not averaged** (a
  stay spanning both a weekday and a weekend night is billed per actual night, not a blended
  rate × nights, which was Phase 3's interim approach). `commissionPct` also resolves live from
  `platform_parking_settings`. **Resolved values are snapshotted onto the
  `parking_payment_transactions` row at creation time** — a later admin config change never
  touches an already-created transaction (see "Platform config & payouts" below).
  `paymongo-webhook` → `handlePaymongoWebhookEvent` dispatches on `metadata.kind ===
'parking_booking'` **first** (checked before the org-subscription path — without this a
  parking webhook would silently no-op against the wrong table) → `fulfillParkingPayment`:
  idempotent (`status === 'paid'` early-return), guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE status =
'PENDING_PAYMENT'` to `PENDING_REVIEW`, **then** sends `sendParkingConfirmedEmail` (moved here
  from claim-time). If the booking already moved on by the time the webhook lands (released by
  a timeout race), the transaction is still marked `paid` with a manual-review flag instead of
  forcing a status flip — never creates a second paid reservation for one request.
- **Payment window times out**: `runExpireParkingPayments` (same cron tick as
  `runExpireParkingBroadcasts`, `expire-parking-broadcasts` endpoint — no separate `pg_cron`
  entry) sweeps `parking_payment_expires_at`, calls `releaseParkingClaim` then
  `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch` — **resumes the search** (next batch, or terminate once
  exhausted). The guest didn't ask to stop.
- **Guest cancels**: `cancel-parking-booking` → `cancelParkingBooking`
  (`parkingCancellation.ts`) — while `PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE`, straight to `CANCELLED`; while
  `PENDING_PAYMENT`, calls the **same** `releaseParkingClaim` primitive but then sets
  `CANCELLED` instead of resuming — **the guest explicitly asked to stop**, this must never
  fall through to `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`.

`releaseParkingClaim` (`parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts`) is the shared low-level "un-claim"
primitive both paths above call — it never decides what happens next, only the caller does. Do
not add a third caller that skips this split.

## Anti-spam (Phase 3 fast-follow)

`parkingAntiSpam.ts#assertParkingSubmitAllowed` — locked v1 constants (overview D15, not
admin-configurable): max `PARKING_MAX_CONCURRENT_PENDING` (3) live requests
(`PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE`/`PENDING_PAYMENT`) per `guest_auth_user_id`, and a
`PARKING_CANCELLATION_COOLDOWN_HOURS` (24h) cooldown after
`PARKING_CANCELLATION_COOLDOWN_THRESHOLD` (3) cancellations in that window. Called from
`submit-parking-booking-request` **only when `guestEmail` matches the caller's own email** — a
host submitting via the admin "New booking" modal (see "Guest sign-in requirement" above) is
never rate-limited against their own account for creating bookings on guests' behalf. IP/device
throttling is still deferred — the endpoint is guest-authenticated now, which already narrows
that surface; revisit once Phase 8's unauthenticated direct-link entry point exists.

## Platform config & payouts (Phase 4)

- **Config resolver**: `parkingPlatformSettings.ts#resolveParkingPlatformSettings()` is the
  single source of truth for `commissionPct`/`guestRateWeekday`/`guestRateWeekend`, reading the
  singleton `platform_parking_settings` row (`id = 1` CHECK, mirrors `platform_payment_settings`).
  Every caller (`parkingBroadcastRanking.ts` for the cap, `parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts` for
  payment amounts, `parkingPricing.ts` for the host-facing cap + display) resolves it **once per
  operation** and threads the values through — never re-query per candidate/night.
- **Super-admin config page**: `platform-parking-settings` edge function (GET/PUT singleton,
  `serveSuperAdmin`, mirrors `platform-payment-settings`) + `SuperAdminParkingPayoutsPage.tsx`
  (`/admin/parking/payouts`). Changing commission/guest rate here only affects bookings created
  **after** saving — see the snapshot invariant above.
- **Host-readable cap**: hosts can't call the super-admin-gated settings endpoint, so
  `parking-pricing` GET piggybacks the live cap (`guestRateCapWeekday`/`guestRateCapWeekend`)
  and `commissionPct` onto its own response (`ParkingPricingDto`) for
  `ParkingPricingRatesFormCard.tsx`'s inline warning + fee/net-payout display.
  `parkingPricingDefaults.ts`'s `STUB_*` constants are fallback-only now (used only before the
  real response loads) — never the enforcement source.
- **Payout ledger — manual disbursement only**: `parking_payment_transactions` (Phase 3) gained
  `disbursed_at`/`disbursed_by`/`disbursement_reference`/`disbursement_method` (default
  `'manual'` — `'paymongo_platforms'` is reserved for when real PayMongo Platforms split-payout
  ships, not yet built) and `clawback_amount`/`clawback_reason`/`clawback_at`/`clawback_by`
  (audit trail only, no automated collection). `parking-payouts` edge function
  (`serveSuperAdmin`): GET lists `status = 'paid'` transactions; PATCH with
  `{action: 'mark_disbursed', transactionId, reference?}` or `{action: 'record_clawback',
transactionId, amount, reason}` — mirrors `org-subscriptions-admin`'s GET/PATCH action-dispatch
  shape.
- **Out of scope until PayMongo Platforms business/compliance work lands**: real automated
  split-payout, host KYC onboarding, PayMongo's real fee schedule, volume eligibility threshold —
  these require directly contacting PayMongo, not code. Don't build a "real payout" API path
  ahead of that.

## Endorsement automation & communication (Phase 5)

- **Endorsement ≠ confirmation email.** `sendParkingEndorsementEmail()`
  (`parkingEndorsementEmail.ts`) is addressed to the matching development's PMO (approval to let
  the guest's vehicle onsite), CC guest — distinct from `sendParkingConfirmedEmail()`
  (`parkingBroadcastEmail.ts`), the guest-facing "you're confirmed" notice. Both fire from the
  same `fulfillParkingPayment()` payment-success path in `parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts`, each in
  its own isolated `try/catch` — a Resend outage on either must never fail payment fulfillment or
  cascade into marking the transaction `failed`.
- **PMO recipient resolution**: a parking has no dedicated recipient config — the send resolves
  the PMO email via `loadDevelopmentPmoEmailByName(supabase, parking.residence_name)`
  (`developmentSerialize.ts`), matching against `developments.name`. If no matching development
  row (or no `pmoEmail` on it) exists, the send throws `ParkingEndorsementRecipientError` — this
  becomes `endorsement_send_error`, a concrete, fixable reason (configure the development's PMO
  email), not a silent failure.
- **Idempotency**: `guest_submissions.endorsement_sent_at` is the guard — every write (success or
  failure path) is a guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE endorsement_sent_at IS NULL`. First successful send
  wins; a later retry (webhook double-fire, or the guest's manual resend racing the auto-send)
  can never overwrite an already-sent record. On success, `endorsement_email_snapshot` stores the
  **exact rendered HTML** sent — the guest-facing "view copy" panel renders this stored snapshot
  verbatim, never a re-render (which could drift if templates change later).
- **Guest resend**: `request-parking-endorsement` edge function
  (`requestParkingEndorsementResend()`) — same ownership check as `cancel-parking-booking`
  (`guest_auth_user_id === user.id`), only usable once the booking is past payment
  (`PENDING_REVIEW`/`READY_FOR_CHECKIN`/`COMPLETED`) and no send has succeeded yet.
- **Auto-accept**: `parking_settings.automation_toggles.autoAcceptTopMatch` (extends the existing
  JSONB automation-toggle bag from Phase 2/3's email toggles — no new column). Checked only
  against the **initial** batch's top candidate, in `submit-parking-booking-request/index.ts`
  right after `fanOutParkingBroadcast()` — calls the exact same `claimParkingBooking()` primitive
  the manual `claim-parking-booking` endpoint uses, so first-accept-wins safety is untouched. A
  re-batch after a decline/timeout does **not** re-check auto-accept (v1 scope — see file map doc
  for why: hooking it inside `fanOutParkingBroadcast()` itself would create a circular import
  between `parkingBroadcast.ts` → `parkingBroadcastActions.ts` → `parkingBroadcastExpireCron.ts` →
  `parkingBroadcast.ts`).
- **Post-match chat reuses existing infra, not a new system.** The guest-facing web chat widget
  (`ui/src/features/guest/chat/`) already exists and already accepts a `parkingSlug` — it's
  scoped per `(parking, guest_user_id)` via `social_conversations`, not per booking. `ParkingChatSheet.tsx`
  is a thin wrapper around that existing `useGuestChatResume`/`useGuestChatStart`/`GuestChatThread`
  stack (skipping the inquiry-specific FAQ/date-picker/voice-session pieces that don't apply
  post-booking). The chat CTA is gated client-side on `endorsementSentAt` being set — the
  underlying thread itself isn't booking-scoped, so a guest with multiple sequential bookings at
  the same parking shares one thread across them. Accepted v1 limitation; do **not** add a
  `booking_id` column to `social_conversations` speculatively — only if this proves to be a real
  problem.
- **Contact reveal is guest-sees-host-contact only.** `resolveParkingHostContact()`
  (`parkingBroadcast.ts`) — reuses `resolveParkingHostRecipients()`'s owner-first candidate pool,
  enriched with `parking_members.display_name`/`contact_phone`. `get-parking-booking-status`
  includes this only when `endorsement_sent_at IS NOT NULL`. The host side (guest email/phone on
  `ParkingBookingDetailPage.tsx`) was already unconditional before this phase and is intentionally
  **not** gated — that's baseline booking info the host needs for on-site verification, not part
  of the "post-match communication" contact-sharing concept.
- **Admin escalation contact**: `platform_parking_settings.support_escalation_phone` (extends
  Phase 4's singleton config + `/admin/parking/payouts` page) — surfaced on the guest status page
  **unconditionally**, regardless of chat/endorsement state.

## Property-booking migration (Phase 7)

- **`guest_submissions.linked_property_booking_id`** — set only on a `parking_id` row, pointing
  at a `property_id` row it was self-served from. Self-referencing FK on the same table (property
  vs. parking rows are mutually exclusive via a `property_id`/`parking_id` CHECK constraint).
  Ownership + linkability are verified in `submit-parking-booking-request` at insert time
  (`parkingPropertyLink.ts#verifyLinkablePropertyBooking`), not enforced by a DB constraint — same
  RLS-is-permissive-here convention as the rest of this table.
- **Linkability ≠ stay-guide eligibility.** `isParkingLinkableStatus()` allows `PENDING_DOCUMENTS`
  or later (excludes `PENDING_REVIEW`/`CANCELLED`/`IMPORTED`) — deliberately earlier than the
  RFCI+ stay-guide gate, because linking needs to work well before check-in. It matches the two
  status shapes `transition-booking`'s same-status `document_completion_target` call can actually
  act on (`PENDING_DOCUMENTS` same-status, or the RFCI+ "late parking" rule above) — see the
  file's own comment for the residual gap on legacy `PENDING_GAF`/`PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST`/
  `PENDING_PET_REQUEST` literal statuses.
- **Self-serve entry**: `list-linkable-property-bookings` (guest-authenticated) resolves the
  signed-in guest's linkable stays by `guest_user_id`/`guest_email` — same identity match as
  `guestProfileService.ts#listGuestTrips`, deliberately reimplemented rather than imported to keep
  this marketplace module decoupled from the guest-portal trips list. `ParkingRegistrationForm.tsx`
  shows a "which stay is this for?" picker (single match auto-selects) and prefills unit + vehicle
  fields only — **not** check-in/out dates, since a pinned listing's dates come from that
  listing's own availability calendar, not the property stay (prefilling them could silently
  submit dates the listing isn't actually available for).
- **Auto-complete**: `parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts#fulfillParkingPayment`, after a successful
  payment, if `linked_property_booking_id` is set, reads that property booking's **current**
  status and calls `WorkflowOrchestrator.transition()` same-status with
  `document_completion_target: 'PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST'` — the same call
  `ParkingRequestForm.tsx`'s manual "Mark as Complete" makes, never a raw column write. Isolated
  try/catch (mirrors the endorsement email send in the same function) — a failure here never
  fails the parking payment, and is not retried. Fires a `booking_parking_matched` in-app
  notification on success.
- **Property booking detail panel**: `get-linked-parking-booking` (property-scoped read, mirrors
  `get-booking-ai-review`'s `resolveScopedPropertyAccess` + `verifyBookingBelongsToProperty`
  pattern) resolves the linked booking's status/endorsement/host contact via
  `resolveParkingHostContact()`. `ParkingPanel.tsx` renders this when linked, else the legacy
  owner/rate fields unchanged — never both.
- **Host-assist share link**: `useBookingParkingShareLink.ts` + `useOwnerDefaultParking` /
  `resolve-owner-default-parking`. When the property’s org has an **available** own parking for
  the stay dates, primary share/open uses `guestParkingOwnDefaultPath`
  (`/parkings/:slug/form?linkStay=…&checkInDate=…&checkOutDate=…`); otherwise
  `guestParkingFindPath` (`/parkings?linkStay=…`). Host **Use your parking** / **Find parking**
  opens that URL; **Search other parkings** always opens marketplace browse. Already-linked stays
  open the request status page. Legacy pay-parking URLs redirect via `PayParkingPage` +
  `get-pay-parking` (prefer own-default when available). Multi-slot: booking detail opens
  `OwnerParkingConfirmSheet`. Ranking: `preferredOwnerParkingId` (property settings) → same
  `residence_name` → earliest `created_at`.
- **Same-org owner-owned auto-claim**: `submit-parking-booking-request` — when `parkingId` is
  pinned **and** `linkedPropertyBookingId` is set **and** both belong to the same
  `organization_id` (`isSameOrgOwnerOwnedPin`), fan-out inserts broadcast rows with
  `skipNotify: true` then immediately `claimParkingBooking` → `PENDING_PAYMENT` (no Accept
  self-notify). If the linked property has `complimentaryOwnerParking: true`,
  `claimParkingBooking` skips the awaiting-payment guest email, then
  `fulfillComplimentaryOwnerParking` confirms with a ₱0 `provider: complimentary`
  ledger row (endorsement + property gate) — no PayMongo. Cross-org / unlinked pins keep the
  normal Accept path. Occupancy for defaults includes `PENDING_PAYMENT` and in-flight
  `parking_pinned_id` requests. Large orgs: occupancy `.in(parking_id, …)` / pinned-id lookups
  use `postgrestInChunks` so resolution does not fail with **URI too long**.
- **Guest parking CTAs (emails / reminders)**: `resolveGuestParkingCtaAbsoluteUrl` — booking
  acknowledgement and `parkingReminderCron` prefer own-default form deep links when an org
  slot is available for the stay; otherwise stay-scoped `/parkings?linkStay=…`.
- **Host-on-behalf ownership (Phase B)**: pay/cancel/endorsement accept caller email matching
  `guest_email` and rebind `guest_auth_user_id` (`parkingGuestOwnership.ts`) so Admin New booking
  guests can self-serve after signing in with the booking email.
- **Pre-arrival reminder**: `send-parking-reminders` cron (`parkingReminderCron.ts`, daily,
  `parking-reminder-daily` job) — one-time reminder (dedupe: `parking_reminder_sent_at`) to any
  linkable, unlinked, `need_parking = true` property booking within 3 days of check-in.
  CTA URL uses `resolveGuestParkingCtaAbsoluteUrl` (own-default when available).
- **Legacy broadcast retirement**: `workflowOrchestrator.ts` no longer calls
  `sendParkingBroadcast()` on a new `need_parking` signal (see `.cursor/rules/booking-workflow.mdc`).
  `submit-pay-parking` remains for historical tooling only — host **Find parking** no longer opens
  the vehicle form.

## Direct-booking link (Phase 8)

- **Reuses the existing pinned-listing route** — no new landing page. A host's shareable link is
  `/parkings/:slug/form?dl=<token>`, the same route Phase 2's pinned single-round submit already
  uses; the `?dl=` marker is the only new thing riding along.
- **Still guest-authenticated.** Do not build an anonymous/unauthenticated variant of this path —
  Phase 3 already made every parking submit require guest sign-in (ownership binding for
  pay-now/cancel, plus `parkingAntiSpam.ts`'s per-account limits), and those protections apply to
  a direct-link submission exactly the same way. The link only changes which commission rate
  applies, never the auth requirement.
- **Token generation/verification**: `parkingDirectLink.ts`. `ensureParkingDirectBookingToken`
  lazily generates and persists `parkings.direct_booking_token` (two concatenated
  `crypto.randomUUID()`s, same pattern as `parkingTeamService.ts`'s invite tokens) the first time
  a host's dashboard requests it (`parking-pricing` GET) — idempotent, never regenerated on
  subsequent calls. `resolveParkingBookingChannel` verifies a guest-supplied token server-side
  against the pinned parking's stored token at submit time; a missing or mismatched token is
  **never an error** — it silently resolves to `'standard'`. Don't ever trust a client-supplied
  channel/discount flag directly.
- **Channel snapshot, same discipline as commission_pct**: `guest_submissions.parking_booking_channel`
  is set once, at submit time, in `submit-parking-booking-request`. It is read once at payment-link
  creation (`parkingPaymentOrchestrator.ts#createParkingPaymentTransaction`) to pick
  `direct_commission_pct` vs `commission_pct`
  (`computeParkingPaymentAmounts`'s new `bookingChannel` param), then that resolved rate is
  snapshotted onto `parking_payment_transactions.booking_channel` — don't re-derive the channel by
  joining back to `guest_submissions` later, the transaction row is the permanent record.
- **Anti-spam scope is narrower than a naive "public link" read would suggest** — see the phase
  doc's decision #4 write-up. Only `get-public-parking` (the read-only landing lookup) got a new
  per-IP rate limit (`checkIpRateLimit`, mirrors `search-suggestions`); the authenticated submit
  endpoint itself was **not** given a separate IP throttle — the existing per-account limit already
  covers it, and stacking an IP limit on top would risk penalizing legitimate guests behind a
  shared IP (hotel/condo wifi) for no real additional protection.

## Multi-tenancy

Candidate queries filter by `organization_id` at the source (`findParkingBroadcastCandidates`).
Every host-facing endpoint (`claim`, `decline`, `get-parking-broadcast-status`,
`transition-parking-booking`) re-verifies access via `verifyParkingTeamAccess` scoped to the
**specific `parkingId` in the request**, not just "any authenticated org member" — never trust
a client-supplied `organizationId` for authorization, only for candidate matching.

## Guest status surface

`get-parking-booking-status` (public/anon) takes a booking UUID (unguessable, bearer-capability
style) and returns a narrow projection — no listing/enumeration endpoint exists, and it 404s
identically whether the row doesn't exist or isn't a parking row. The guest status page
(`ParkingRequestStatusPage.tsx`) **polls every 4s**, not Supabase Realtime — this is a
documented deviation from the original "locked" Realtime decision in
`parking-e2e-phase1-guest-request-realtime-status.md`; it was kept because it already satisfies
that doc's own ≤5s fallback acceptance bar. If true Realtime is ever implemented, it needs a
`guest_auth_user_id` column + RLS-scoped channel per that doc's "locked approach" section — do
not silently half-implement it.

**Non-refundable notice** (`NonRefundableNotice` in `ParkingRequestStatusView.tsx`) is a single
component mounted at two conditions — `status === 'PENDING_PAYMENT'` (pre-payment) and `isPaid`
(persistent post-payment) — which together cover all three touchpoints the policy asks for
("before payment, payment confirmation, ongoing status page"), since this app has no separate
payment-confirmation page (PayMongo redirects back to this same status view).

## Notification deep links

Both Telegram and email host notifications deep-link straight to
`/org/:orgSlug/parking/:parkingSlug/bookings/:bookingId` (`ParkingBookingDetailPage`) — not the
bare bookings list. Telegram has no button/CTA affordance, so the link is appended as plain text
after the templated message body (not part of the user-editable template).

## Host dashboard

`ParkingBookingDetailPage.tsx` shows Accept/Decline only when
`broadcastStatus.response === 'pending'` for **this** parking (`useParkingBroadcastStatus`).
`BookingRow.parking_broadcast_expires_at` (already returned by `select('*')` / list-bookings —
just was missing from the TS type) drives `ParkingBroadcastCountdown`
(`ui/src/features/dashboard/bookings/components/ParkingBroadcastCountdown.tsx`), shown next to
the status badge on the detail page, list table, and card grid whenever status is
`PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE` — this is the host's only urgency signal while racing to Accept, keep
it wired whenever `BookingRow` or the broadcast payload shape changes.

