## Don'ts

- Don't route `PENDING_HOST_ACCEPTANCE` through `transition-parking-booking` — it's explicitly
  blocked; use claim/decline/expire.
- Don't add a second write path to `guest_submissions.status` for the terminal transitions —
  the guarded UPDATE pattern is what makes emails/notifications exactly-once.
- Don't trust a client-supplied `organizationId`/`parkingId` for authorization — always
  re-verify via `verifyParkingTeamAccess` scoped to the specific parking in the request.
- Don't add a "settings UI" for the TTL cron cadence unless product actually asks for a
  configurable schedule — it's intentionally fixed at 5 min, unlike the Telegram cron jobs.
- Don't reimplement the batch-advance-or-terminate guard per-caller — always call
  `advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`, the same way claim/decline/expire never reimplement the
  claim-win guard.
- Don't invent per-booking guest-selected check-in/check-out times for the turnover buffer —
  it's sourced from the listing's own standard times (`parkings.settings.checkInTime`/
  `checkOutTime`), not the guest form.
- Don't call `releaseParkingClaim` without immediately deciding what happens next — a timeout
  resumes the search (`advanceOrTerminateParkingBatch`), a guest cancel terminates
  (`CANCELLED`). Never let a release silently fall through to the wrong outcome.
- Don't add a new webhook branch that skips the `metadata.kind` check in
  `handlePaymongoWebhookEvent` — every kind must be dispatched explicitly, never assumed by
  fallthrough (that's exactly the bug this rule replaced).
- Don't send `sendParkingConfirmedEmail` from claim — it fires from `fulfillParkingPayment` on
  payment success only; claim sends `sendParkingAwaitingPaymentEmail` instead.
- Don't hardcode a guest rate/commission constant anywhere new — resolve
  `resolveParkingPlatformSettings()` instead, and don't recompute it retroactively for an
  already-created `parking_payment_transactions` row; the values are snapshotted at checkout
  creation on purpose (a later admin config change must never move a paid or in-flight
  transaction's numbers).
- Don't build a real automated split-payout path yet — `disbursement_method` stays `'manual'`
  until PayMongo Platforms business/compliance work actually lands; the ledger is a manual
  disburse/clawback audit trail only.
- Don't trust a client-supplied `directLinkToken`/channel flag directly — always verify it
  server-side against `parkings.direct_booking_token` via `resolveParkingBookingChannel`. A
  missing/mismatched token silently falls back to `'standard'`, never an error.
- Don't build an unauthenticated variant of the direct-booking-link submit path — guest auth is
  already required for every parking submission (Phase 3) and that protection applies here too;
  see the Phase 8 doc's decision #4 write-up before "fixing" this to be more literally
  "unauthenticated."
